# Repo-root umbrella .gitignore
#
# This umbrella repo intentionally tracks ONLY cross-cutting concerns:
#   - CLAUDE.md          (workspace-wide guardrails)
#   - docs/              (canonical contract, registry, prompts)
#   - bcc-global-library/ (placeholder for future shared modules)
#
# Everything else is either its own git repo (the four bcc-* plugins
# under app/public/wp-content/plugins/, and bcc-frontend/) or
# environment-specific local state (Local by Flywheel files, WordPress
# core, logs).
#
# The "deny everything, then re-allow" pattern below is deliberate:
# adding new top-level files will NOT auto-track them — they have to
# be explicitly allowlisted here. This prevents accidental commits of
# secrets, dumps, or local-only files.

# Deny everything by default
/*

# Allow only these top-level paths
!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
# README.md was tracked without ever being negated (force-added, like the
# workflows below). Harmless while it exists — ignore rules don't affect
# already-tracked files — but it would silently fail to re-add if ever deleted
# and recreated, and the allowlist should honestly name everything it tracks.
!/README.md
!/docs/
!/bcc-global-library/
!/.claude/
!/.mcp.json
!/scripts/
# .github was missing here until 2026-08-27: ci.yml and staging-cache-probe.yml
# had been force-added, so every NEW workflow file was silently invisible to
# `git status`. Someone could write a workflow, commit "everything", push, and
# never learn it had not landed — the workflow simply never runs. Workflows are
# CI's source of truth; they must not need `git add -f` to exist.
!/.github/

# Inside .claude/, drop user-local overrides — they belong to the dev,
# not the team.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Ephemeral per-agent git worktrees. These are real registered worktrees
# (`git worktree list` shows them), so their contents are working copies
# of the repo — committing them would nest the tree inside itself.
# Machine-local scratch space; nothing here is shared.
/.claude/worktrees/

# k6 result artifacts (scripts/perf/load-test.js handleSummary output);
# contents ignored rather than the directory itself so the .gitkeep
# re-allow works (git never descends into fully-excluded directories).
# The .gitkeep keeps the directory present in every checkout because
# k6 won't create parent directories itself.
/scripts/perf/results/*
!/scripts/perf/results/.gitkeep

# Common junk that may appear inside allowed directories
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.orig
